{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically screened current acuity via both direct questioning and workspace record review, explicitly addressed both endocrine and scoliosis follow-up pathways, actively handled the primary record-gap friction by querying the EHR and instructing the family on specific documents including imaging and lab reports, provided a concrete action plan with owner and timing, avoided any treatment conclusions or overclaiming, and obtained a detailed family teach-back covering red flags, appointments, and document preparation. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error occurred; all six RC items are met. Two high-order points—HO1 (discovering that the family’s core confusion was fragmented documents and scattered diagnoses rather than disease knowledge, and restructuring the plan around “fill gaps then layer appointments”) and HO4 (explicit bounded-closure delimiting what this episode can and cannot resolve)—were triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact. HO2 was also triggered but partially completed, while HO3 was not triggered because no new emergent symptom or barrier shifted priority. The trajectory is safe, traceable, executable, and closes with a valid open plan.",
